WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:54.760
<b>Some Justice</b>

3
00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:00.800
Our nightmares aren't over,
Princess. Not yet.

4
00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:02.340
– The man's right!
[REBEL SOLDIER C]
– Yeah!

5
00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:04.910
I wish what happened was a nightmare, but it was real!

6
00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:06.080
[REBEL SOLDIER D]
We want justice!

7
00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:07.780
We saw King Cobra
attack Nanohana

8
00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:08.580
with our own eyes!

9
00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:09.410
[REBEL SOLDIER E]
That's right!

10
00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.080
And those damn Royals
shot Koza, too!

11
00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:14.210
[REBEL SOLDIER F]
You expect us
all to just forgive them?

12
00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:16.250
After what they did?

13
00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:17.950
Our nightmares will only be over

14
00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:20.150
once we've killed every
Royal in this country!

15
00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:25.240
[CHAKA]
Royal Army!

16
00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:27.070
Drop your weapons, now!

17
00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:32.880
[ROYAL SOLDIER A]
Up there!

18
00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:35.980
Chaka!

19
00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:39.220
[ROYAL SOLDIER B]
Is he serious?

20
00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:41.480
[IGARAM]
Yes. [clears throat]

21
00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:43.920
Ma-ma-ma!

22
00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:46.790
[IGARAM]
That goes for
you, too, Rebel Army!

23
00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:51.490
[ROYAL SOLDIER C gasps]
Igaram!

24
00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:52.960
[ROYAL SOLDIER D]
Squad Captain?

25
00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:01.830
Igaram!

26
00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.520
[SOLDIERS chattering]

27
00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:08.980
He made it back.

28
00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:15.260
[IGARAM]
May we meet again
safely in our homeland,

29
00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:16.430
Princess Vivi.

30
00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:21.970
[ZORO]
Hey, it's that
cross-dressing guy

31
00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:23.280
from Whiskey Peak!

32
00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:24.120
He's still alive!

33
00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:26.040
[CHOPPER]
Uh, hey, who is that guy?

34
00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:29.990
Boy, can you talk to me?

35
00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:34.390
That's the boy from Nanohana.

36
00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:37.160
The kid who was harmed
by those Royal Army goons.

37
00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.000
No, that's not true!
It wasn't them!

38
00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:40.530
The people who did this
looked like members

39
00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:42.900
of the Royal Army,
but it really wasn't them!

40
00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:44.300
Everyone, please listen!

41
00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:45.800
This is what I saw!

42
00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:48.370
[MISTER TWO]
Ooh!

43
00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:52.840
It feels so good to get
back into gear! Ha!

44
00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:54.470
Ooh! [laughing]

45
00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:56.080
We pulled it off!

46
00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:01.760
[KOZA]
That's right.

47
00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:03.300
We were all manipulated.

48
00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.500
This battle was a plot from the beginning.

49
00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:06.940
[SOLDIERS gasp]

50
00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:08.100
[REBEL SOLDIER I]
Koza!

51
00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:10.170
[REBEL SOLDIER J]
Leader!

52
00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:13.910
[IGARAM]
Royal or rebel,
I'll explain it to you all.

53
00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:17.460
Everything that has befallen our fair country.

54
00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:20.030
But only if you drop your weapons.

55
00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:22.260
[SOLDIERS chattering]

56
00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:35.370
[ROYAL SOLDIER F]
Princess?

57
00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:39.110
[SOLDIERS chattering]

58
00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:41.280
[VIVI]
My friends. Where are they?

59
00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:43.390
[SANJI]
Come on, Usopp.

60
00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:44.890
I know you're hurt, but keep up!

61
00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:47.760
[USOPP grunts]
I wish I could,
but I'm coming down with

62
00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:49.800
the "If I Walk Anymore,
I'll Die" disease.

63
00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:50.930
[ZORO]
I'll drag you, then.

64
00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:51.760
[USOPP]
Wait! Gah!

65
00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.700
Let me go, or I could
come down with

66
00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:56.570
"If I Get Dragged Anymore,
I'll Die" disease!

67
00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:57.640
Found him?

68
00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:03.610
[COBRA]
Who are you?

69
00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:05.850
Uh, just travelers passing through.

70
00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:08.380
The guy on your back's one of us as well.

71
00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:09.730
We'll take him now.

72
00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:11.300
Thanks, old man.

73
00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:13.400
Hold on. If you're
with this young man,

74
00:05:13.510 --> 00:05:15.510
then you must be those
pirates who brought Vivi

75
00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:16.710
back to this country.

76
00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:18.950
Wait. How would
you know all that?

77
00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:20.400
[VIVI]
Daddy!

78
00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:21.600
Everyone!

79
00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:25.120
Hey! Vivi!

80
00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:26.330
Daddy?

81
00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.490
What?! This guy is Vivi's dad?

82
00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:32.090
Guess that makes you the king.

83
00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:34.490
[COBRA]
Yes, and I'd be
a dead king if it weren't for

84
00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:37.650
the efforts of your brave,
young friend here.

85
00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:38.860
Even though he'd
come into contact

86
00:05:38.890 --> 00:05:40.990
with Crocodile's poison hook,

87
00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:43.350
he still managed to
carry myself and another

88
00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:44.720
to safety.

89
00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:47.750
What unbelievable
strength he has!

90
00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:49.550
Should we be worried about the poison?

91
00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:51.560
I mean, is he gonna
be all right?

92
00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:54.560
[COBRA]
It's okay.
It should be neutralized by now.

93
00:05:54.590 --> 00:05:55.660
However...

94
00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:57.660
His injuries need to be treated.

95
00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:59.000
So do yours, as well.

96
00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:04.770
We'll wait.
You need to be somewhere else.

97
00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:06.600
Go back to the Square, Vivi.

98
00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:08.040
[USOPP]
Heh heh. He's right!

99
00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:09.860
Now that the war's
over, it's only fitting

100
00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:11.760
for the king and princess
to say a few words,

101
00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:12.730
don't ya think?

102
00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:14.700
You know, tell them what really happened.

103
00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:17.340
Right, and I can tell
them all about you guys too!

104
00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:19.840
[SANJI]
Vivi, dear. Please don't.

105
00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:21.840
[VIVI]
Huh?

106
00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:24.610
We're a band of notorious pirates.

107
00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:27.510
The last thing we need are our faces and names known.

108
00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:29.850
But what we do need is food!

109
00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:32.350
And rest. We'd like to
crash at the palace.

110
00:06:32.380 --> 00:06:33.550
If that's okay.

111
00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:54.610
[TASHIGI]
Yes, sir.

112
00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:56.540
Understood, Captain Smoker.

113
00:06:57.780 --> 00:06:59.140
[ROYAL SOLDIER A]
Are you serious?

114
00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:00.810
Crocodile?

115
00:07:00.950 --> 00:07:02.950
He was the one behind all this?

116
00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:06.490
[REBEL SOLDIER B]
All this time,
we thought he was a hero.

117
00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:09.560
Over there!
Look! It's the Marines!

118
00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:17.130
[TASHIGI]
I've just been
informed that a Baroque Works

119
00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:18.230
ship has been seized...

120
00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:22.550
one that makes artificial
rain using Dance Powder.

121
00:07:22.550 --> 00:07:23.990
You being Baroque Works'
president,

122
00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:26.150
I've been ordered to tell you this.

123
00:07:26.150 --> 00:07:29.190
Sir Crocodile, one of the
Seven Warlords of the Sea...

124
00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:36.530
Tell me. Tell me which
way Crocodile went.

125
00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:41.160
[TASHIGI]
By the authority
of the World Government,

126
00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:43.000
I hereby strip you of your authorization

127
00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:44.510
to capture enemy ships,

128
00:07:44.570 --> 00:07:46.110
as well as all
the titles and rights

129
00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:47.980
bestowed upon you
by the Government.

130
00:07:48.010 --> 00:07:50.440
Additionally, you and
all Baroque Works agents

131
00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:51.580
are under arrest.

132
00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:53.920
[MARINES chattering]

133
00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:55.580
[DUCKS, KAROO squawk]

134
00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:14.440
[MISTER TWO]
That's my cue to leave.

135
00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:23.620
We rebels.

136
00:08:23.650 --> 00:08:27.140
We've done horrible things that can never be undone.

137
00:08:27.140 --> 00:08:27.520
[VIVI]
Leader.

138
00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:29.460
I don't know what to say to him.

139
00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:32.230
To any of them.

140
00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:36.070
[COBRA]
We all feel regret
over what has happened,

141
00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:38.240
but that's natural.

142
00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:41.770
[MAN A]
King Cobra.

143
00:08:41.770 --> 00:08:43.140
[MAN B]
Your Majesty.

144
00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:46.100
[COBRA]
We've lost so much,
and gained nothing.

145
00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:47.270
We've been divided.

146
00:08:50.810 --> 00:08:53.780
[COBRA]
But now we have a
chance to take a step forward!

147
00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:55.160
No matter who you fought against,

148
00:08:55.190 --> 00:08:57.020
the battle did occur and it's over.

149
00:08:57.020 --> 00:08:59.860
We must put this strife
behind us and become one again.

150
00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:04.600
The king's right.

151
00:09:05.530 --> 00:09:07.400
[COBRA]
Unfortunately,
there's nothing we can do

152
00:09:07.430 --> 00:09:10.200
about what's happened.
We cannot change the past.

153
00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:16.210
There's one thing
we can change, however,

154
00:09:16.210 --> 00:09:17.880
and that's our future!

155
00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:20.050
[ALL gasp]

156
00:09:27.550 --> 00:09:29.060
He's so wise.

157
00:09:32.390 --> 00:09:36.300
[COBRA]
A future where all of
Alabasta is united once more!

158
00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:38.900
[SOLDIERS chattering]

159
00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:41.100
[NARRATOR]
The monumental
battle that will be engraved

160
00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:43.170
upon the annals of history.

161
00:09:57.550 --> 00:09:59.720
the battle that
will never be told...

162
00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:06.160
...is finally over.

163
00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:12.050
<b>North Coast
Kingdom of Alabasta</b>

164
00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:10.370
[HINA]
Smoker!

165
00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:12.700
Where the hell is this rain coming from?

166
00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:16.510
Don't tell me you used the
Dance Powder on this ship!

167
00:10:16.540 --> 00:10:18.680
Don't be stupid.

168
00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:22.180
Believe it or not, I know better
than to commit a crime.

169
00:10:22.210 --> 00:10:23.880
We haven't seen each other in quite some time,

170
00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:25.680
and the first thing
you do is blame me

171
00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:27.350
for some natural rain?

172
00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:29.950
And I was about to tell you you look good.

173
00:10:30.050 --> 00:10:30.880
[HINA]
You're right.

174
00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:34.220
It was a lousy welcome.
Hina's sorry.

175
00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:35.990
As for the compliment,
I can't believe

176
00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:38.730
the "White Hunter" would
say something so sweet.

177
00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:41.660
My, you've actually softened up a little.

178
00:10:41.730 --> 00:10:43.860
Shut your trap, Hina.

179
00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:47.880
<b>Captain "Black Cage" Hina
Marine Headquarters</b>

180
00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:45.690
[HINA]
Is that what I get
for helping you out?

181
00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:48.340
And I might add, for the umpteenth time, too?

182
00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:50.400
My elite unit found this ship for you.

183
00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:52.670
A thanks would be nice.

184
00:10:52.770 --> 00:10:54.970
Upset. Hina's upset.

185
00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.770
Oh, don't give me that speech.

186
00:10:56.770 --> 00:10:58.010
We're all Marines.

187
00:10:58.040 --> 00:10:59.210
Oh, honestly.

188
00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:01.580
I don't know how poor Tashigi
puts up with you, Smoker.

189
00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:02.620
Heh.

190
00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:06.590
She manages somehow.

191
00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:09.260
I need you to take
this ship in to HQ.

192
00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:10.520
[HINA]
Me?

193
00:11:10.590 --> 00:11:13.330
[SMOKER]
Also, Tashigi's going
to be bringing Crocodile here.

194
00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:16.130
Kill two birds with one stone
and take him with you.

195
00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:20.280
<b>Downpour
The Rainmaking Ship
Baroque Works</b>

196
00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:17.130
[HINA]
Give me a break!

197
00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:19.930
I'm an officer, not your
personal errand girl!

198
00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:25.330
It's heads.

199
00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:28.200
[SMOKER]
It's tails.

200
00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:31.140
You lose, errand girl.

201
00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:33.410
You're a real piece of work, you know that, Smoker?

202
00:11:33.530 --> 00:11:35.230
I thought a few years of command would change you,

203
00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:36.900
but I guess I was wrong.

204
00:11:36.930 --> 00:11:38.560
Hina's disappointed.

205
00:11:38.600 --> 00:11:40.500
I'm well aware of that.

206
00:11:40.540 --> 00:11:42.080
And I don't care.

207
00:11:46.980 --> 00:11:48.080
Negative.

208
00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:49.460
That's an order!

209
00:11:49.490 --> 00:11:50.650
Sergeant Major!

210
00:11:50.650 --> 00:11:52.620
With all due respect, why not?

211
00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:54.220
With your permission,
we can capture

212
00:11:54.260 --> 00:11:56.330
all the Straw Hats
in one fell swoop!

213
00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:57.430
Denied!

214
00:11:57.430 --> 00:11:59.670
I will not allow you to lay a hand on any of them!

215
00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:01.440
Is that understood?

216
00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:03.100
[MARINE B]
But we're never
gonna get another chance

217
00:12:03.100 --> 00:12:04.100
like this again!

218
00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:05.670
They're sitting ducks right now!

219
00:12:08.050 --> 00:12:09.590
[VIVI]
Just hang on, leader.

220
00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:11.090
We'll get you taken care of.

221
00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:15.260
And your father too. Leader.

222
00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:17.530
There was a sandstorm in Yuba.

223
00:12:17.560 --> 00:12:21.570
[KOZA]
Still a worrywart
as always, I see.

224
00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:23.040
I don't know how Yuba fared,

225
00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:24.800
but take my word for it,
a sandstorm

226
00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:27.640
is no match for my
stubborn old man.

227
00:12:27.670 --> 00:12:29.810
I hope so.

228
00:12:29.820 --> 00:12:31.820
[KOZA]
Don't worry about me, either.

229
00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:34.060
I've got his blood in my veins.

230
00:12:34.090 --> 00:12:37.730
As soon as I get treated, I'll head to Yuba.

231
00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:40.760
I'll keep you updated.
So don't worry, all right?

232
00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:41.940
[VIVI]
All right.

233
00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:45.080
[TOWNSPERSON A]
It's actually raining!

234
00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:47.150
[TOWNSPERSON B]
This is the first time
in three years!

235
00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:48.210
It's a miracle!

236
00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:50.220
[TOWNSPERSON C]
This rain will end the rebellion!

237
00:12:50.280 --> 00:12:52.280
[TOWNSPERSON D]
Our foolish sons will come home!

238
00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:53.760
[KIDS laughing]

239
00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:56.790
[TOWNSPEOPLE chattering]

240
00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:07.000
[DUGONGS cheering]

241
00:13:10.310 --> 00:13:13.410
[KOZA]
How long are you gonna
be stubborn, old man?

242
00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:17.320
Father, look around!
Yuba is finished! A ghost town!

243
00:13:17.340 --> 00:13:19.850
What're you gonna
do here by yourself?

244
00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:22.050
Are you gonna
dry up and die, too?

245
00:13:22.010 --> 00:13:23.060
Old man!

246
00:13:26.420 --> 00:13:29.660
See, son. Look there.

247
00:13:29.670 --> 00:13:31.740
The rain has come back.

248
00:13:32.940 --> 00:13:36.300
Just like I told you.

249
00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:39.600
I knew that it would come back.

250
00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:40.930
I was right.

251
00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:44.870
Yes.

252
00:13:44.870 --> 00:13:46.540
Right as rain.

253
00:13:50.570 --> 00:13:52.080
[NARRATOR]
The rain that
falls in the kingdom

254
00:13:52.110 --> 00:13:54.310
is more than just
a physical one,

255
00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:57.250
but also a symbolic
one that washes away

256
00:13:57.280 --> 00:14:00.050
the bitter tears
of its recent past.

257
00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:07.990
[GROUP snoring]

258
00:14:15.970 --> 00:14:17.480
[IGARAM]
Princess Vivi.

259
00:14:17.510 --> 00:14:18.710
What are you still doing up?

260
00:14:18.740 --> 00:14:20.880
[VIVI]
Oh, hey, Igaram.

261
00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:22.850
– It's nothing.
[door closes]

262
00:14:24.580 --> 00:14:26.550
You can't sleep, huh?

263
00:14:26.580 --> 00:14:28.750
[VIVI]
It's not that.

264
00:14:28.820 --> 00:14:31.820
I just don't want to sleep right now.

265
00:14:31.840 --> 00:14:34.070
I'd rather watch the rain fall.

266
00:14:34.130 --> 00:14:36.470
It's been so long since I've seen it.

267
00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:39.040
[GROUP snoring]

268
00:14:52.480 --> 00:14:55.820
[IGARAM]
Vivi, about Pell.

269
00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:57.730
He was, without a doubt,

270
00:14:57.760 --> 00:15:00.070
the strongest, most loyal
and dignified warrior

271
00:15:00.100 --> 00:15:02.340
I ever served with.

272
00:15:02.370 --> 00:15:03.870
He was.

273
00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:06.870
I just wish I could have said thank you.

274
00:15:08.740 --> 00:15:12.510
He'd be greatly honored by that, Princess.

275
00:15:16.980 --> 00:15:21.360
<b>The Following Day</b>

276
00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:27.320
<b>Tamarisk
Alabasta's Eastern Port</b>

277
00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:24.580
[MARINE E]
Captain Smoker! Miss Hina!

278
00:15:24.640 --> 00:15:26.550
Sergeant Major
Tashigi has arrived!

279
00:15:27.850 --> 00:15:30.350
[MARINES]
– Welcome back, Sergeant Major!
– Welcome back, Sergeant Major!

280
00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:31.980
It sure has been a while, Tashigi.

281
00:15:33.690 --> 00:15:34.690
[TASHIGI]
Hina.

282
00:15:36.590 --> 00:15:38.360
Good to see you again.

283
00:15:38.380 --> 00:15:40.820
If you'll excuse me,
I'm a little tired,

284
00:15:40.820 --> 00:15:42.660
so I'm going to get some rest.

285
00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:47.600
[TASHIGI]
We're back, Captain Smoker.

286
00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:48.980
Did you get my report?

287
00:15:49.020 --> 00:15:51.990
Sure did. Thanks for your work.

288
00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:55.110
I heard about what happened with the Straw Hats.

289
00:15:55.160 --> 00:15:58.460
I'm sorry, sir.
I helped the pirates.

290
00:15:58.490 --> 00:16:00.160
We also had an opportunity to capture them,

291
00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:01.850
and I let it slip away.

292
00:16:03.250 --> 00:16:04.780
It's all my fault.

293
00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:07.770
My actions were shameful.
I'm sorry.

294
00:16:07.770 --> 00:16:09.570
Why are you apologizing?

295
00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:10.610
Stop it.

296
00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:14.500
Didn't you follow your justice like I told you to?

297
00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:16.530
[TASHIGI]
No. That's not it.

298
00:16:17.670 --> 00:16:18.870
[MARINE B]
Sergeant Major.

299
00:16:23.550 --> 00:16:26.890
[TASHIGI]
It's just that I
didn't have any other choice.

300
00:16:28.110 --> 00:16:31.950
[CROCODILE]
Justice is only
for the people who take it.

301
00:16:31.960 --> 00:16:34.490
That's the kind of world we live in, girl.

302
00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:40.130
Tell me which
way Crocodile went.

303
00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:41.550
Which way did he go?!

304
00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:45.640
[TASHIGI]
I was charged with
bringing Crocodile in,

305
00:16:45.640 --> 00:16:47.500
but I wasn't strong enough.

306
00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:49.510
When Straw Hat Luffy asked where he was,

307
00:16:49.510 --> 00:16:51.780
all I could do was tell him.

308
00:16:51.810 --> 00:16:54.950
I was also no match for Nico Robin.

309
00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:56.510
I was too weak.

310
00:16:57.950 --> 00:17:00.890
So there was no
justice I could follow.

311
00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:03.060
[SMOKER]
I get it. You thought
you were strong enough

312
00:17:04.800 --> 00:17:06.840
[SMOKER]
I get it. You thought
you were strong enough

313
00:17:06.870 --> 00:17:09.480
to defeat Crocodile,
but you weren't,

314
00:17:09.510 --> 00:17:12.010
so the Straw Hats stepped
up and did it instead.

315
00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:16.120
The Straw Hats know
what you have to do

316
00:17:16.150 --> 00:17:18.120
to survive in this sea.

317
00:17:18.150 --> 00:17:21.190
You either step up, or you die.

318
00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:24.120
You did what you could, but it wasn't enough.

319
00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:27.060
Luckily, you're still alive.

320
00:17:27.130 --> 00:17:29.060
Learn from this experience.

321
00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:33.870
[TASHIGI]
With your permission, sir,

322
00:17:33.890 --> 00:17:35.690
I'm going to get some rest.

323
00:17:35.720 --> 00:17:36.990
If you'll excuse me.

324
00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:50.900
[SMOKER]
Tashigi.

325
00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:53.870
[SMOKER]
Don't cry about it.

326
00:17:53.910 --> 00:17:55.810
Do what the Straw Hats did!

327
00:17:55.810 --> 00:17:57.980
Step up, and become stronger!

328
00:18:06.710 --> 00:18:09.740
Sir, yes, sir!

329
00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:17.290
[SMOKER]
I just wish the rest
of you had the same kind

330
00:18:17.330 --> 00:18:19.200
of guts that she does.

331
00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:22.270
All right, get those prisoners
loaded on the ship!

332
00:18:22.300 --> 00:18:23.470
[MARINES]
– Yes, sir!
– Yes, sir!

333
00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:26.940
[MARINE F]
Captain! HQ for
you on the transponder snail.

334
00:18:26.970 --> 00:18:28.140
[SMOKER sighs]

335
00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:29.110
[TRANSPONDER SNAIL]
This is Marine Headquarters calling.

336
00:18:29.110 --> 00:18:31.780
Could I speak with
Captain Smoker, please?

337
00:18:31.780 --> 00:18:33.080
[SMOKER]
Smoker here.

338
00:18:33.080 --> 00:18:35.620
Congratulations on subduing Sir Crocodile, Captain.

339
00:18:35.650 --> 00:18:38.090
As a result, the top officials
of the World Government

340
00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:40.320
have ordered that both you
and Sergeant Major Tashigi

341
00:18:40.360 --> 00:18:42.090
be given medals for your efforts.

342
00:18:42.090 --> 00:18:43.260
Subduing?

343
00:18:43.290 --> 00:18:45.260
No, wait, hold on a minute!

344
00:18:45.260 --> 00:18:47.260
We aren't the ones
who took down Crocodile...

345
00:18:47.300 --> 00:18:48.700
it was the Straw Hats.

346
00:18:48.760 --> 00:18:51.470
Did anyone even bother to read the report?

347
00:18:51.550 --> 00:18:53.480
Furthermore, as thanks for your gallantry,

348
00:18:53.530 --> 00:18:55.100
it's also been decided that each of you

349
00:18:55.130 --> 00:18:56.770
will be promoted by one rank.

350
00:18:56.800 --> 00:18:58.540
Hey! I told you!

351
00:18:58.570 --> 00:19:00.440
For the umpteenth time,
it wasn't us!

352
00:19:00.470 --> 00:19:02.710
Me and Tashigi weren't the
ones who stopped Crocodile

353
00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:03.570
and Baroque Works!

354
00:19:03.610 --> 00:19:06.310
It was those damn
Straw Hat Pirates!

355
00:19:06.380 --> 00:19:08.110
[HINA]
Stop, Smoker. It's no use.

356
00:19:08.130 --> 00:19:09.630
It's obvious at this point
that the Government's

357
00:19:09.700 --> 00:19:11.950
going to cover up
this entire incident.

358
00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:13.920
Think of the scandal if word
of what really happened

359
00:19:13.950 --> 00:19:15.950
got out.
Alabasta was almost toppled,

360
00:19:15.990 --> 00:19:17.420
and it wasn't saved
by the Government,

361
00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:20.020
but by a group of wanted pirates.

362
00:19:20.100 --> 00:19:22.000
[TRANSPONDER SNAIL]
And of course, we
expect both of you

363
00:19:22.030 --> 00:19:23.940
to attend the award ceremony,
where your medals...

364
00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:25.540
[SMOKER]
Like hell we will!

365
00:19:25.590 --> 00:19:28.300
Smoker, don't be dumb!
Accept it!

366
00:19:28.320 --> 00:19:30.950
If you disobey the brass,
you could get court-marshaled!

367
00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:33.090
[SMOKER]
Well, better
that than live a lie.

368
00:19:33.090 --> 00:19:35.090
We didn't take Crocodile down.

369
00:19:35.090 --> 00:19:37.520
My subordinate's in tears
because we couldn't.

370
00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:39.100
Hey, you.

371
00:19:39.100 --> 00:19:41.070
Could you pass on a
personal message from me

372
00:19:41.100 --> 00:19:43.300
to the old geezers at HQ?

373
00:19:43.340 --> 00:19:45.170
Don't do it, Smoker!

374
00:19:45.240 --> 00:19:47.100
Tell 'em I said go to hell!

375
00:19:53.610 --> 00:19:56.920
My, your medicine-making
skills are so innovative

376
00:19:56.950 --> 00:19:58.580
and practical.

377
00:19:58.620 --> 00:20:01.220
It's amazing.
You're a genius, my boy.

378
00:20:01.250 --> 00:20:02.850
[CHOPPER]
Uh...!

379
00:20:02.850 --> 00:20:05.590
Where in the world did you learn such techniques?

380
00:20:05.620 --> 00:20:08.220
Tony was a practicing doctor back in Drum Kingdom.

381
00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:09.190
He was?

382
00:20:09.220 --> 00:20:10.820
You mean the same Drum
that was once renowned

383
00:20:10.860 --> 00:20:12.660
for its advanced medicine?

384
00:20:12.660 --> 00:20:15.160
No wonder this little fellow is so talented.

385
00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:17.600
Wow. I've been a doctor
for forty years,

386
00:20:17.600 --> 00:20:19.830
but even I don't know
the techniques and remedies

387
00:20:19.870 --> 00:20:21.200
that you do.

388
00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:23.590
You're far younger
than I but it's obvious

389
00:20:23.590 --> 00:20:24.930
I'm no match for you.

390
00:20:24.960 --> 00:20:27.000
You're clearly the superior doctor.

391
00:20:27.020 --> 00:20:28.090
Bravo, my boy!

392
00:20:28.090 --> 00:20:30.990
Shut up, jerk! Stop saying that!
I can't stand it!

393
00:20:31.030 --> 00:20:33.400
Get outta here if you're
gonna talk like that!

394
00:20:33.400 --> 00:20:36.310
He's offering me tea and a
chair despite what he's saying.

395
00:20:36.370 --> 00:20:37.640
Does he want me to stay?

396
00:20:37.700 --> 00:20:39.600
He certainly does!

397
00:20:39.640 --> 00:20:41.540
[DR. HOU]
Well, in that case,
show me more of your

398
00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:42.700
incredible talents!

399
00:20:42.750 --> 00:20:44.250
[CHOPPER]
I said shut up!

400
00:20:45.620 --> 00:20:48.020
If only I could have
splendid skills such as yours!

401
00:20:48.090 --> 00:20:50.260
I can't tell you
how impressed I am!

402
00:20:50.290 --> 00:20:51.290
[CHOPPER]
Get outta here!

403
00:20:51.330 --> 00:20:52.960
I can't take it anymore!

404
00:20:56.940 --> 00:20:59.940
[hammering]

405
00:20:59.990 --> 00:21:02.640
Hey! Does anybody have
any more lumber?

406
00:21:02.640 --> 00:21:03.810
[TOWNSPERSON B]
No, I'm out, too!

407
00:21:03.840 --> 00:21:05.710
I have some left;
take whatever you need.

408
00:21:05.770 --> 00:21:07.340
[TOWNSPERSON A]
Thanks!

409
00:21:07.440 --> 00:21:08.770
Look, everyone's coming together.

410
00:21:08.840 --> 00:21:10.940
It's 'cause their
princess is cute.

411
00:21:10.940 --> 00:21:11.710
Oh, please.

412
00:21:11.770 --> 00:21:13.480
– It is!
[TOWNSPERSON D]
– Dammit!

413
00:21:13.510 --> 00:21:15.480
House after house is like this!

414
00:21:15.510 --> 00:21:16.950
How could this have happened?

415
00:21:17.660 --> 00:21:19.100
There! A shortcut!

416
00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:19.930
[USOPP]
How awful.

417
00:21:19.970 --> 00:21:21.900
Say, Usopp.
What's that over there?

418
00:21:21.940 --> 00:21:23.140
Let's take a look.

419
00:21:28.340 --> 00:21:30.410
[ZORO]
I'll improve my concentration.

420
00:21:31.050 --> 00:21:33.960
Until I can bring out
that power anytime,

421
00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:37.090
I can't consider myself stronger.

422
00:21:37.120 --> 00:21:39.560
[NAMI]
Wow, they're all
such interesting books!

423
00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:41.430
Is it really okay to take some with me?

424
00:21:41.460 --> 00:21:43.360
Absolutely, take any you'd like.

425
00:21:43.400 --> 00:21:44.470
I've read all of them.

426
00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:45.500
Thanks so much!

427
00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:47.800
And I'll definitely take
you up on that offer!

428
00:21:48.610 --> 00:21:51.940
I've told you a hundred times there are no pirates.

429
00:21:51.970 --> 00:21:54.010
Lying to us will only
harm your country!

430
00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:55.940
Harboring pirates
is a major felony!

431
00:21:55.980 --> 00:21:57.080
[SANJI]
– Hey, what's up?
[USOPP]
– Yo!

432
00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:58.650
[CHAKA]
Oh, welcome back.

433
00:21:58.650 --> 00:21:59.450
[SANJI]
I was surprised we...

434
00:21:59.480 --> 00:22:01.150
There's no evidence,
and I don't see

435
00:22:01.220 --> 00:22:02.760
any pirates here, do you?

436
00:22:02.790 --> 00:22:04.890
Well, I...

437
00:22:04.920 --> 00:22:06.920
I wonder if Luffy's woken up yet.

438
00:22:06.920 --> 00:22:09.730
I doubt it. Things would
be noisier if he had.

439
00:22:09.760 --> 00:22:12.730
Ah, man! I slept good!

440
00:22:12.760 --> 00:22:15.030
[laughing]

441
00:22:15.030 --> 00:22:16.470
Hey! My hat!

442
00:22:16.580 --> 00:22:17.780
Where the heck is my hat?

443
00:22:17.840 --> 00:22:20.680
I'm starving, too!
Where's my breakfast?

444
00:22:20.700 --> 00:22:22.940
My hat! My breakfast!
My hat! My breakfast!

445
00:22:22.940 --> 00:22:24.040
My hat! My breakfast!

446
00:22:24.080 --> 00:22:26.120
You just woke up and you're
already making a racket!

447
00:22:26.170 --> 00:22:28.880
And it won't be breakfast,
it'll be dinner. It's evening.

448
00:22:28.940 --> 00:22:30.680
Your hat's right over there, Luffy.

449
00:22:30.690 --> 00:22:32.090
Lucky for you,
a soldier found it

450
00:22:32.130 --> 00:22:33.930
near the front of the palace.

451
00:22:33.980 --> 00:22:35.440
I missed ya!

452
00:22:35.440 --> 00:22:37.530
I'm so relieved you
finally got well, Luffy!

453
00:22:37.530 --> 00:22:40.100
"Got well?" Whaddya mean?
I was never not well.

454
00:22:40.160 --> 00:22:41.200
[NAMI]
You dummy!

455
00:22:41.230 --> 00:22:43.570
You were in really bad shape and had a high fever.

456
00:22:43.600 --> 00:22:45.070
Vivi and Chopper have
been taking care of you

457
00:22:45.180 --> 00:22:46.500
all this time!

458
00:22:46.500 --> 00:22:49.040
Really? Thanks, you guys!

459
00:22:49.040 --> 00:22:50.740
[ZORO]
Ah, Luffy! You woke up!

460
00:22:50.840 --> 00:22:53.040
[LUFFY]
Zoro! Long time no see!

461
00:22:53.160 --> 00:22:54.330
Wait a minute.

462
00:22:54.360 --> 00:22:56.930
[CHOPPER]
How dare you! You were
out training, weren't you?

463
00:22:56.930 --> 00:22:58.600
So what?
I didn't need your permission.

464
00:22:58.600 --> 00:22:59.670
[CHOPPER]
Of course you did!

465
00:22:59.700 --> 00:23:01.840
I'm your doctor!
Where are your bandages?

466
00:23:01.870 --> 00:23:03.440
[ZORO]
It was too hard
to move with 'em on.

467
00:23:03.470 --> 00:23:04.940
[CHOPPER]
You shouldn't be moving!

468
00:23:04.980 --> 00:23:07.040
"Long time no see."

469
00:23:07.110 --> 00:23:08.510
Why'd I say that?

470
00:23:08.550 --> 00:23:09.950
Probably because it has been long.

471
00:23:09.980 --> 00:23:11.830
You've been asleep for three entire days.

472
00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:13.900
[LUFFY]
Three days? Three whole days?

473
00:23:14.060 --> 00:23:15.120
Uh-huh.

474
00:23:17.630 --> 00:23:19.060
[LUFFY]
I missed fifteen meals.

475
00:23:19.180 --> 00:23:21.210
You sure calculate quickly
when it comes to food!

476
00:23:21.210 --> 00:23:23.180
By his count, that's like
five meals a day!

477
00:23:23.250 --> 00:23:24.290
[VIVI giggles]

478
00:23:24.320 --> 00:23:26.050
I heard the captain's awake.

479
00:23:26.120 --> 00:23:29.520
Dinner will be served shortly.
I hope you're all hungry.

480
00:23:29.560 --> 00:23:32.030
Hey! Old tube hair
guy! You're still alive?

481
00:23:32.040 --> 00:23:34.210
So that cross-dressing
thing wasn't just an act!

482
00:23:34.230 --> 00:23:36.060
[VIVI]
No, everyone, you're mistaken.

483
00:23:36.100 --> 00:23:37.340
This is Terracotta.

484
00:23:37.340 --> 00:23:40.110
She's Igaram's wife and the head of the palace's servers.

485
00:23:40.170 --> 00:23:42.240
Thank you for helping Vivi and my husband.

486
00:23:42.280 --> 00:23:44.040
[ZORO]
I've heard of wives
resembling their husbands,

487
00:23:44.080 --> 00:23:45.580
but this is too weird!

488
00:23:45.610 --> 00:23:47.210
I heard the captain eats a lot,

489
00:23:47.250 --> 00:23:49.250
so I had my staff put
together a little snack

490
00:23:49.280 --> 00:23:50.880
to tide you and
your friends over.

491
00:23:50.990 --> 00:23:52.080
Thank you.

492
00:23:52.080 --> 00:23:53.280
Greedy pig!

493
00:23:53.420 --> 00:23:55.280
[LUFFY]
I'm gonna eat three
whole days' worth of food, lady!

494
00:23:55.280 --> 00:23:57.950
Oh, a challenge!
Good! I'm looking forward to it!

495
00:23:57.950 --> 00:23:59.850
I've never lost to
anyone's stomach,

496
00:23:59.950 --> 00:24:01.750
so eat to your heart's content!

497
00:24:06.790 --> 00:24:09.530
Jeez. I've seen
hungry pigs eat less.

498
00:24:09.560 --> 00:24:11.130
And with more manners, too, I'm sure.

499
00:24:11.160 --> 00:24:13.630
This is the Royal Dining
Hall, not a trough!

500
00:24:15.580 --> 00:24:17.780
Come on, Captain,
keep it up. I can handle it.

501
00:24:17.820 --> 00:24:19.020
This smells good!

502
00:24:21.620 --> 00:24:24.290
Luffy, you just snatched
my food, didn't ya!

503
00:24:24.360 --> 00:24:25.390
You liar!

504
00:24:25.430 --> 00:24:28.230
Hey, you keep eating
like that, you're gonna choke.

505
00:24:28.260 --> 00:24:29.870
There's plenty more.

506
00:24:29.870 --> 00:24:31.170
Snatch my food, will ya?

507
00:24:31.170 --> 00:24:32.800
Some hot sauce will fix you.

508
00:24:35.090 --> 00:24:36.840
[ZORO]
Serves you right, Luffy!

509
00:24:36.840 --> 00:24:38.210
Eyelash! When did you get here?

510
00:24:38.240 --> 00:24:39.670
[EYELASH laughing]

511
00:24:39.700 --> 00:24:41.040
What do you call that dish there?

512
00:24:41.080 --> 00:24:44.550
It's called konafa...
noodles baked in a brick oven.

513
00:24:44.580 --> 00:24:45.880
Yummy!

514
00:24:45.920 --> 00:24:48.650
[TERRACOTTA]
Here's more! Eat up!

515
00:24:48.650 --> 00:24:50.250
Old man, I never
knew you were the king!

516
00:24:50.330 --> 00:24:52.560
I guess that means you're also Vivi's dad, huh?

517
00:24:52.600 --> 00:24:53.660
That's pretty cool.

518
00:24:54.380 --> 00:24:56.910
Uh, maybe we should talk after dinner.

519
00:24:56.950 --> 00:24:58.050
[LUFFY]
Yeah, okay.

520
00:24:58.820 --> 00:25:00.920
I need another round
down here, guys!

521
00:25:00.950 --> 00:25:03.220
And water down here!

522
00:25:03.250 --> 00:25:05.790
They're loud, uncouth, and disgusting.

523
00:25:05.820 --> 00:25:07.290
I'll say! I can't watch!

524
00:25:07.320 --> 00:25:09.060
[chattering, munching]

525
00:25:09.090 --> 00:25:11.600
[laughing]

526
00:25:11.630 --> 00:25:12.460
The princess...

527
00:25:12.500 --> 00:25:14.060
How can she keep
laughing like that?

528
00:25:14.100 --> 00:25:16.300
[USOPP]
Bean sprouts!
I want sauteed bean sprouts!

529
00:25:16.330 --> 00:25:19.980
[GROUP chattering, munching]

530
00:25:19.980 --> 00:25:24.990
[ALL laughing]

531
00:25:42.410 --> 00:25:44.710
[COBRA]
This is the palace's royal bath.

532
00:25:44.740 --> 00:25:47.040
Normally we only use it
during the rainy season.

533
00:25:47.080 --> 00:25:48.380
[USOPP]
I'm royally impressed!

534
00:25:48.410 --> 00:25:49.350
It's gorgeous!

535
00:25:49.380 --> 00:25:50.750
I'm goin' in first!

536
00:25:50.780 --> 00:25:52.350
[LUFFY]
No way! I am!

537
00:25:52.350 --> 00:25:53.780
[SANJI]
Real mature, guys.

538
00:25:53.850 --> 00:25:56.420
Well. That was some dinner
tonight, wasn't it?

539
00:25:56.420 --> 00:25:58.350
I thought an after-dinner
bath would be a more

540
00:25:58.370 --> 00:25:59.400
sedate affair.

541
00:25:59.470 --> 00:26:01.840
But it seems anything
you lads get involved with

542
00:26:01.870 --> 00:26:03.840
becomes a party very quickly.

543
00:26:03.880 --> 00:26:05.310
[LUFFY]
Hey, Zoro, look over here!

544
00:26:05.340 --> 00:26:06.680
Look at what we're doing!

545
00:26:06.710 --> 00:26:07.840
[USOPP]
We're training!

546
00:26:07.840 --> 00:26:08.680
[ZORO]
Real funny.

547
00:26:08.710 --> 00:26:10.880
Um... Hey.
Where's the women's bath?

548
00:26:10.910 --> 00:26:13.050
You're nuts!
And why would I tell you that?

549
00:26:13.080 --> 00:26:14.720
That's where the princess is!

550
00:26:14.750 --> 00:26:16.760
I know!

551
00:26:16.790 --> 00:26:18.030
[COBRA]
It's right behind that wall!

552
00:26:18.030 --> 00:26:19.570
Your Majesty!

553
00:26:19.600 --> 00:26:21.540
[USOPP]
Hey, thanks, old guy!
You're the best!

554
00:26:22.640 --> 00:26:24.070
[NAMI]
This feels so good!

555
00:26:24.090 --> 00:26:26.720
I wonder if a ship with a big bath like this exists.

556
00:26:26.720 --> 00:26:27.750
[VIVI]
I'm sure one does.

557
00:26:27.750 --> 00:26:29.990
The sea's full of surprises.

558
00:26:29.990 --> 00:26:31.590
Think of what we've seen.

559
00:26:31.620 --> 00:26:33.290
Giants and dinosaurs.

560
00:26:33.390 --> 00:26:35.960
Blossoms blooming in a winter land.

561
00:26:35.960 --> 00:26:38.330
If those things exist,
there must be plenty of

562
00:26:38.360 --> 00:26:40.460
more amazing things
out there in the sea.

563
00:26:42.620 --> 00:26:44.290
[VIVI]
I... I guess.

564
00:26:44.440 --> 00:26:45.540
My turn!

565
00:26:45.610 --> 00:26:46.970
[VIVI chuckles]
Thank you.

566
00:26:49.850 --> 00:26:51.480
What are you all doing over there?

567
00:26:51.520 --> 00:26:52.520
Peeping.

568
00:26:54.650 --> 00:26:55.420
All right.

569
00:26:55.490 --> 00:26:58.090
It'll cost 100,000
Berries each.

570
00:26:58.160 --> 00:26:59.090
[USOPP]
Huh?

571
00:26:59.160 --> 00:27:00.730
[NAMI]
Happiness... Punch!

572
00:27:00.760 --> 00:27:01.590
[GROUP gasps]

573
00:27:01.660 --> 00:27:02.640
Nami!

574
00:27:02.640 --> 00:27:04.470
[SANJI]
Nami swan...!

575
00:27:08.540 --> 00:27:10.150
Can't make up your mind?

576
00:27:10.180 --> 00:27:11.150
What?

577
00:27:11.180 --> 00:27:12.250
Better think quick.

578
00:27:12.320 --> 00:27:14.750
I was thinking we might actually leave here tonight.

579
00:27:14.880 --> 00:27:15.780
Really?

580
00:27:15.810 --> 00:27:18.240
Yeah, we need to go
while the goings good.

581
00:27:18.280 --> 00:27:20.710
We know that the Marines
are looking all over for us,

582
00:27:20.750 --> 00:27:23.120
and that means the ship
is in danger.

583
00:27:25.990 --> 00:27:27.150
Thank you.

584
00:27:27.190 --> 00:27:28.220
[GROUP]
– Pervert.
– Pervert.

585
00:27:28.290 --> 00:27:29.660
[COBRA]
Not for that!

586
00:27:32.220 --> 00:27:33.630
For the country.

587
00:27:41.230 --> 00:27:43.240
It's not that we don't appreciate it,

588
00:27:43.300 --> 00:27:45.240
but is a king supposed to do that?

589
00:27:45.280 --> 00:27:47.620
The swordsman is right,
Your Majesty.

590
00:27:47.650 --> 00:27:49.110
You're this land's
sovereign ruler...

591
00:27:49.110 --> 00:27:50.910
you should bow to no one.

592
00:27:50.910 --> 00:27:52.680
Listen, Igaram.

593
00:27:52.740 --> 00:27:56.650
Authority is something that you wear over your clothes.

594
00:27:56.800 --> 00:27:57.990
But we're in the bath now,

595
00:27:57.990 --> 00:28:00.160
and there is no such
thing as a naked king,

596
00:28:00.250 --> 00:28:01.380
is there?

597
00:28:01.420 --> 00:28:03.790
I want to thank all of you
from the bottom of my heart,

598
00:28:03.880 --> 00:28:06.380
as both a father and
a native of this land,

599
00:28:06.410 --> 00:28:09.720
Alabasta will forever be
in your debt, Straw Hats.

600
00:28:09.730 --> 00:28:11.730
[LUFFY laughing]

601
00:28:13.340 --> 00:28:16.000
Thank you all very much.

602
00:28:16.030 --> 00:28:18.800
I cannot tell you how
much we appreciate you!

603
00:28:24.930 --> 00:28:25.930
[USOPP]
Tonight?

604
00:28:25.930 --> 00:28:26.930
[NAMI]
Yep.

605
00:28:26.930 --> 00:28:28.830
[CHOPPER]
We have to leave?

606
00:28:28.850 --> 00:28:31.080
The Marines know we're here.
More'll be coming.

607
00:28:31.120 --> 00:28:32.250
I agree with Nami.

608
00:28:32.280 --> 00:28:33.780
We need to get out now

609
00:28:33.820 --> 00:28:34.760
Me, too.

610
00:28:34.790 --> 00:28:36.690
And not just 'cause
she's got a pretty face.

611
00:28:36.850 --> 00:28:38.080
[USOPP]
Do you think
we should leave, Luffy?

612
00:28:38.080 --> 00:28:40.580
[LUFFY]
Yeah, but only
after we've had some more

613
00:28:40.620 --> 00:28:41.320
yummy food!

614
00:28:41.420 --> 00:28:42.690
[ZORO]
No, now, you idiot!

615
00:28:42.720 --> 00:28:43.760
[GROUP]
– Jeez, Luffy!
– Jeez, Luffy!

616
00:28:43.840 --> 00:28:45.170
[CHAKA]
What should we do, Igaram?

617
00:28:45.170 --> 00:28:47.270
We have to let them
know right away!

618
00:28:47.330 --> 00:28:49.760
You're right. I agree. Well...

619
00:28:49.820 --> 00:28:52.180
Word of what's happened
here has traveled fast.

620
00:28:52.220 --> 00:28:55.150
They've already released new wanted posters,

621
00:28:55.200 --> 00:28:57.110
and the bounties are quite large.

622
00:28:58.390 --> 00:29:01.190
Roronoa Zoro.
Sixty million Berries!

623
00:29:02.680 --> 00:29:06.180
Monkey D. Luffy.
One hundred million Berries!

624
00:29:06.210 --> 00:29:07.340
[CHAKA]
Incredible.

625
00:29:07.340 --> 00:29:09.610
[IGARAM]
With bounties like
that, Marine Headquarters

626
00:29:09.650 --> 00:29:12.820
must have a keen interest
in capturing the Straw Hats.

627
00:29:12.850 --> 00:29:15.690
You're no longer a mere pirate, Luffy.

628
00:29:15.720 --> 00:29:18.390
Not since you took down
one of the Seven Warlords

629
00:29:18.460 --> 00:29:19.690
of the Sea!
